From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:45:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: poll the FIFO every microsecond, not every 200

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

NovaOS (Rigol DHO800/DHO900, MHO900; RK3399) local patch: in PIO (FIFO)
mode, which SPL uses on RK3399 for SDMMC0 (u-boot,spl-fifo-mode),
dwmci_fifo_ready() slept 200 us on every empty-FIFO poll. A 1 KiB FIFO
refills in about 40 us at 49.5 MHz x 4 bit, so the read rate fell to about
4 MB/s and a 1 MB u-boot.itb took about 0.25 s. The poll now sleeps 1 us;
the 4 s limit is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/dw_mmc.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/dw_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/dw_mmc.c
index c2424d78..5efab5f6 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/dw_mmc.c
@@ -183,11 +183,17 @@ static void dwmci_prepare_data(struct dwmci_host *host, struct mmc_data *data,
 
 static int dwmci_fifo_ready(struct dwmci_host *host, u32 bit, u32 *len)
 {
-	u32 timeout = 20000;
+	/*
+	 * Poll every microsecond, not every 200: the bus refills a drained
+	 * 1 KiB FIFO in about 40 us at 50 MHz x 4 bit, so a 200 us sleep per
+	 * empty poll held SPL's PIO reads to about 4 MB/s. The limit stays
+	 * 4 s, as before.
+	 */
+	u32 timeout = 4000000;
 
 	*len = dwmci_readl(host, DWMCI_STATUS);
 	while (--timeout && (*len & bit)) {
-		udelay(200);
+		udelay(1);
 		*len = dwmci_readl(host, DWMCI_STATUS);
 	}
 
